# .gitattributes
#
# MWBM-MEDIA-LANG policy copies must stay byte-for-byte identical to the
# master files in MWBMPartners/MeedyaSuite-core (see
# docs/standards/media-language-bcp47-policy.md, section 8.3). Git can change
# a file's bytes several ways as it moves the file between its stored form
# and the copy on disk: converting line endings, running a filter, converting
# text encoding, or expanding an "$Id$" marker. Any one of those would make
# the copy checker (scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py) report the file as
# "changed" even though nobody edited a single character, so all four are
# turned off below for each copied file:
#   -text                   never convert line endings
#   -filter                 never run a filter on this file
#   -working-tree-encoding  never convert its text encoding
#   -ident                  never expand an "$Id$" marker in it
# These lines can be overridden. Three things win over them:
#   - any later line in this same .gitattributes that also matches the copy
#     (git uses the last matching line for each setting, so that line need
#     not be broader);
#   - a .gitattributes file closer to the copy: one in the copy's own folder,
#     or in a folder between the copy and the top folder of the repository
#     (a deeper file wins over a shallower one; a .gitattributes in some
#     other folder that does not contain the copy has no effect on it);
#   - a person's own ".git/info/attributes" file, because git always gives
#     that file the highest priority.
# The global and system attributes files have the lowest priority, so they do
# not override these lines. If something that does override them changes how
# a copy is written out, the copy checker still catches it, because it
# compares the actual bytes and reports any changed copy; the fix is to
# remove the overriding setting, not to change the copy.
docs/standards/media-language-bcp47-policy.md -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
Tests/Fixtures/bcp47-language-policy-v1.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
Tests/Fixtures/bcp47-language-policy-v1.schema.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
docs/standards/data/bcp47-language-data-v1.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
docs/standards/data/bcp47-language-data-v1.schema.json -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
scripts/media-lang/check_copies.py -text -filter -working-tree-encoding -ident
